==German==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|de|Angst|t1=fear|Hase|t2=hare}}. The compound could be based on the hare’s flight instinct, but is usually thought to be an alteration of unattested {{m|de||*Angsthose}}, from {{m|de|Hose||trousers, pants}}; compare {{cog|de|Bangbüxe}}, {{cog|nl|bangebroek}}, {{cog|en|shit one's pants}}.

